<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sipopa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1876</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sipopa Lutangu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sipopa was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> prince who led the rising of 1864 that overthrew the Kololo rulers of Barotseland, killing most Kololo men and restoring the Lozi monarchy. He then ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a>, but his harsh rule provoked a revolt, and he was killed in 1876.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sipopa.jpg" alt="Sipopa" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seven_Years_in_South_Africa,_page_220,_king_Sepopo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
